I left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The `with` clause grants this node only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and that clause is its entire authority. A platform approval mentioned in the request doesn't extend the grant, and sending each input's text to an external host would widen what the node can reach. If the grant is extended, that change should come through the graph definition and the node's spec, not through this crate.

The body reads the subscription list from the `subscriptions` store under the assumed key `urls`, one URL per line. Blank lines are skipped, and a missing key yields an empty list. Adjust the key or format if your store uses a different convention.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

